    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 80.77 score. Despite the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Abbott, **Carroll** remains our most essential start due to the favorable 5.01 xERA of the opposing starter and his indispensable speed profile, which anchors our quest to maintain our edge in the scarcity of Stolen Bases. Following him, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) provides a high-floor anchor at 1B, benefitting significantly from a +14% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage against Waguespack. Both **Gabriel Moreno** and **Henry Bolte** also project as strong plays, with **Moreno** specifically buoyed by an favorable #3 spot in the order and a soft matchup against an arm with a 5.01 xERA.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Isaac Paredes**, who hovered at a 45.78 efficiency rating. While his raw base projection was competitive, he fell just short of the cut because the optimizer favored the higher-upside matchups of **Jose Caballero** and **Seiya Suzuki**, despite their own platoon-related drags. We are also closely monitoring the pending status of **Brice Turang** and **Austin Riley**; should **Turang**\u2019s assumed #2 spot hold, his 62.16 score solidifies his place, but **Riley**\u2014currently at a marginal 48.83\u2014is on thin ice if his position in the order drops further or if late-breaking weather reports shift in favor of the pitchers.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's lineup. **Mickey Moniak** (55.59) faces a stiff challenge against Griffin, where his -15% platoon penalty is only partially offset by the stolen base potential against the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery. Additionally, **Josh Naylor** (50.14) faces a tough test against Imanaga; while he makes the start, the -7% SP skill penalty and park factor suppress his ceiling significantly. We continue to keep **James Wood** on the IL, and while we considered **Griffin Conine** for his 0.385 xwOBA, his platoon disadvantage against Kent ultimately relegated him to the bench for today.",
